<title>USA: Wall St stocks start softer, Motorola weaker.</title>
<headline>Wall St stocks start softer, Motorola weaker.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. stocks opened modestly softer on Wednesday as Motorola's quarterly earnings warning dampened buying enthusiasm. A still-weak bond market also pressured equities.</p>
<p>The Dow industrials index was down 11 at 5,716. The long bond fell 13/32 to yield 7.15 percent.</p>
</text>
